      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FLYING IN THE WIND (6) has the strongest profile after closing off in Saturday company at Ascot last start, having already won her debut at Bunbury as an odds-on favourite. The move out of an Open into this CL1 suits, and with Pike back aboard, she gets a clear chance to reassert herself third-up. MR MELLON (5) is the main danger on exposed strength, coming through a CL3 at Ascot where he was beaten just over a length as a well-supported favourite, with his Belmont Open fourth two back also reading well. THE LUCKY CHIP (7) comes through a solid form race at this track and trip last start, with three winners coming out of it already from just 5 subsequent starters. He carries no weight again today and third-up here, he can play a role. KAT FIVE (4) resumes after eight months off with two trials behind her and enough 1400m form to run into the minor money if forward enough. FINAL CALL (2) is next best.",
